    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (81.41) stands as our premier offensive anchor, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Michael Lorenzen and a projected move to the #2 spot, which maximizes his elite speed profile in a hunt for scarce stolen bases. **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03) and **Brice Turang** (72.43) provide the highest efficiency scores of our remaining lineup; **Brice Turang** in particular benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Sasaki (5.11 xERA), while **Tyler Soderstrom** gains massive value from a high-upside matchup against Lucas Giolito. **James Wood** (70.10) remains a core start as his leadoff status and strong underlying xwOBA solidify his floor, while **Josh Naylor** (69.73) offers high-leverage production out of the #3 hole against Kolek.\n\nThe optimizer faced a tight decision between **Austin Riley** (67.43) and **Kyle Karros** (51.91) for the final infield slots. While **Austin Riley** carries a high base projection and exploits a slow-delivery pitcher to boost his stolen base potential, **Kyle Karros** ultimately fell to the bench due to the lack of platoon advantage against the right-handed Zac Gallen. We have opted to play it safe with our established starters, as **Travis Bazzana** narrowly missed the 40.0 threshold for starting viability against Zack Wheeler\u2019s elite stuff, and **Jose Caballero** has been removed from consideration entirely due to a rainout. Monitor the lineup cards for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Henry Bolte** closely; while both are currently projected in the low 50s, their status as \"Lineup Pending\" introduces variance should they move deeper into the order or sit out entirely against their respective right-handed matchups.",
